{% doc %}
  blocks/_comparison-column.liquid — private.

  One column of the comparison: the claims down the left, the store's own
  product, or an alternative the customer can switch away from.

  ## One block, three roles, because they are one thing

  
  A claims column, the brand column and an alternative column differ in what
  sits in their top row and in nothing else. All three are a panel with a
  radius, a background and a set of rows divided by a dotted line, and all three
  have to keep those rows in step with each other. Three files would be three
  copies of that, free to drift the first time somebody changes a divider.

  So **Role** chooses the top row:

    Claims       nothing, and the panel starts one row down — which is why the
                 drawing's label column is shorter than the others
    Your product a logo, or a name
    Alternative  the chooser, from which the customer picks a different one

  Everything else is the same set of controls on all three.

  ## It is a `subgrid`, so its padding is inline

  The column is a grid item spanning every row of
  `blocks/_comparison-table.liquid`, with `grid-template-rows: subgrid`. That is
  what keeps *Third-party lab tested* on one line across four columns: the cells
  sit in the table's tracks, not in tracks of this column's own.

  A subgrid's own padding and border are subtracted from its **first and last**
  tracks rather than from every one — so **Top** and **Bottom** here pad the
  header row and the tail of the panel, and the space around a claim is the
  cell's own padding. Left and right behave exactly as they read, and they are
  what insets the dotted divider, because the divider is drawn across the cell's
  content box.

  ## The name is published, not drawn twice

  `data-comparison-name` is how `assets/comparison-table.js` builds every
  chooser's list without the merchant typing the same four names into four
  columns. A block cannot read its siblings in Liquid; the attribute is how one
  reaches another, and it is the same mechanism `<tab-group>` uses to build its
  buttons from its panels.

  Private — the leading underscore — because a comparison column outside a
  comparison table is a panel with nothing to be a column of. It is addable
  inside **Comparison table** and nowhere else.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign s = block.settings

  assign role = s.role | default: 'product'

  comment
    The claims column has no top row in the drawing: its panel begins level with
    the first claim while the product panels start a row higher, and that offset
    is the whole reason the drawing reads as a table with a header. It is a
    checkbox rather than a rule, because a merchant who wants a title over the
    claims should be able to have one.
  endcomment
  assign has_head = true
  if role == 'features' and s.show_head != true
    assign has_head = false
  endif

  assign is_chooser = false
  if role == 'product'
    assign is_chooser = true
  endif

  assign head_source = s.head_source | default: 'logo'
  assign show_logo = false
  if role == 'brand' and head_source == 'logo' and s.logo != blank
    assign show_logo = true
  endif

  assign show_head_text = false
  if has_head and is_chooser == false and show_logo == false
    if s.name != blank and head_source != 'none'
      assign show_head_text = true
    endif
  endif

  comment
    ---- the panel ----

    `color_background`, so a merchant can hand it a gradient — which is what the
    drawing's quiet columns are: a flat mint that is a gradient of one colour in
    Shopify's own picker.

    The alpha goes into the border colour rather than onto the element, for the
    reason `blocks/card-content.liquid` sets out: `opacity` here would fade the
    claims the panel exists to sit behind.
  endcomment
  assign border_line = s.border_style | default: 'none'
  assign border_width = 0
  if border_line != 'none'
    assign border_width = s.border_width | default: 1 | plus: 0
    assign border_percent = s.border_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
    if s.border_color == blank
      assign border_paint = 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor ' | append: border_percent | append: '%, transparent)'
    else
      assign border_alpha = border_percent | divided_by: 100.0
      assign border_paint = s.border_color | color_modify: 'alpha', border_alpha
    endif
  endif

  comment
    ---- corners ----

    Four, twice, behind the same Desktop/Mobile switch the section's own corners
    use. Emitted as one `border-radius` shorthand in the order that property
    takes — top-left, top-right, bottom-right, bottom-left. Each mobile corner
    falls back to its desktop value when the setting is absent entirely.
  endcomment
  assign r_tl = s.radius_top_left | default: 16 | plus: 0
  assign r_tr = s.radius_top_right | default: 16 | plus: 0
  assign r_bl = s.radius_bottom_left | default: 16 | plus: 0
  assign r_br = s.radius_bottom_right | default: 16 | plus: 0

  assign r_tl_m = s.radius_top_left_mobile | default: r_tl | plus: 0
  assign r_tr_m = s.radius_top_right_mobile | default: r_tr | plus: 0
  assign r_bl_m = s.radius_bottom_left_mobile | default: r_bl | plus: 0
  assign r_br_m = s.radius_bottom_right_mobile | default: r_br | plus: 0

  comment
    ---- the divider ----

    Drawn by the cell, configured here, so every row in a column agrees and a
    merchant changes one control rather than six.

    Dashed and dotted are a repeating gradient rather than a `border-style`,
    because CSS gives no control over a border's dash length and the drawing's
    is a precise 2px on, 2px off. A gradient takes both numbers, and `solid`
    falls out of it as a dash with no gap.
  endcomment
  assign divider_style = s.divider_style | default: 'none'
  assign divider_percent = s.divider_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
  if s.divider_color == blank
    assign divider_paint = 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor ' | append: divider_percent | append: '%, transparent)'
  else
    assign divider_alpha = divider_percent | divided_by: 100.0
    assign divider_paint = s.divider_color | color_modify: 'alpha', divider_alpha
  endif

  assign divider_dash = s.divider_dash | default: 2 | plus: 0
  assign divider_gap = s.divider_gap | default: 2 | plus: 0
  if divider_style == 'solid'
    assign divider_gap = 0
  endif
  assign divider_pitch = divider_dash | plus: divider_gap

  assign classes = 'comparison-column comparison-column--' | append: role
  unless has_head
    assign classes = classes | append: ' comparison-column--headless'
  endunless
  if divider_style != 'none'
    assign classes = classes | append: ' comparison-column--ruled'
  endif

  assign column_name = s.name | default: ''

  comment
    Resolved here rather than in the render tag below. A render tag takes bare
    values for its arguments and nothing else — a filter in one is a Liquid
    syntax error that takes the whole file down rather than the one glyph, and
    it is raised at upload rather than at render.

    Note the wording: no tag delimiters are spelled out anywhere in this liquid
    block. A liquid tag ends at the first closing delimiter it meets, including
    one inside a comment line, so writing the tag out here would have closed
    this tag early and left the comment above unterminated. Same hazard
    `snippets/icon.liquid` documents for an svg tag inside a comment.
  endcomment
  assign chevron_px = s.chevron_size | default: 16 | plus: 0
-%}

{%- capture column_style -%}
  {%- render 'spacing', block: s, declarations: true -%}
  --ct-col-radius: {{ r_tl }}px {{ r_tr }}px {{ r_br }}px {{ r_bl }}px;
  --ct-col-radius-mobile: {{ r_tl_m }}px {{ r_tr_m }}px {{ r_br_m }}px {{ r_bl_m }}px;
  --ct-col-border-width: {{ border_width }}px;
  {%- if border_width > 0 -%}
    --ct-col-border-style: {{ border_line }};
    --ct-col-border-color: {{ border_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.background != blank -%}
    --ct-col-background: {{ s.background }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.text_color != blank -%}
    --ct-col-text: {{ s.text_color }};
  {%- endif -%}
  --ct-cell-align: {{ s.cell_alignment | default: 'center' }};
  {%- if divider_style != 'none' -%}
    --ct-divider-height: {{ s.divider_width | default: 1 | plus: 0 }}px;
    --ct-divider-image: repeating-linear-gradient(to right, {{ divider_paint }} 0 {{ divider_dash }}px, transparent {{ divider_dash }}px {{ divider_pitch }}px);
  {%- else -%}
    --ct-divider-height: 0px;
    --ct-divider-image: none;
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if show_logo -%}
    --ct-logo-width: {{ s.logo_width | default: 140 | plus: 0 }}px;
    --ct-logo-width-mobile: {{ s.logo_width_mobile | default: 96 | plus: 0 }}px;
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if show_head_text -%}
    --ct-head-size: {{ s.head_font_size | default: 18 | plus: 0 | divided_by: 10.0 }}rem;
    --ct-head-size-mobile: {{ s.head_font_size_mobile | default: 15 | plus: 0 | divided_by: 10.0 }}rem;
    --ct-head-weight: {{ s.head_font_weight | default: '700' }};
    {%- if s.head_color != blank -%}--ct-head-color: {{ s.head_color }};{%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<div
  class="{{ classes }}"
  data-block-spacing
  data-comparison-column
  data-comparison-role="{{ role }}"
  {%- if column_name != blank %} data-comparison-name="{{ column_name | escape }}"{% endif %}
  {%- if column_name != blank %} role="group" aria-label="{{ column_name | escape }}"{% endif %}
  style="{{ column_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  {%- if has_head -%}
    <div class="comparison-column__head">
      {%- if is_chooser -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          The button is real, named and focusable from the first paint. It
          carries `aria-disabled` rather than `disabled` because without the
          module every alternative column is already on screen — nothing is
          hidden, so nothing is lost, and the control simply has nothing left to
          do. `assets/comparison-table.js` removes the attribute when it takes
          the chooser over.

          The panel is empty in the markup for the reason
          `blocks/_featured-pills-tabs.liquid` gives about its strip: the list is
          the other columns, a block cannot read its siblings in Liquid, and the
          alternative is the merchant keeping one list per column in step by
          hand.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <button
          type="button"
          class="comparison-choose__trigger"
          data-comparison-trigger
          aria-haspopup="listbox"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-disabled="true"
        >
          <span class="comparison-choose__name" data-comparison-trigger-label>
            {{- column_name | default: 'Alternative' | escape -}}
          </span>
          {% render 'icon', icon: 'chevron-down', class: 'comparison-choose__chevron', size: chevron_px %}
        </button>

        <div
          class="comparison-choose__panel"
          data-comparison-panel
          role="listbox"
          tabindex="-1"
          aria-label="{{ column_name | default: 'Alternative' | escape }}"
          hidden
        ></div>
      {%- elsif show_logo -%}
        <div class="comparison-column__logo">
          {% render 'image',
             image: s.logo,
             alt: column_name,
             class: 'comparison-column__logo-image',
             widths: '160,240,320,480',
             sizes: '160px' %}
        </div>
      {%- elsif show_head_text -%}
        <span class="comparison-column__title">{{ column_name | escape }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {% content_for 'blocks' %}
</div>

{%- comment -%}
  Every setting below is a control a merchant reaches in the editor, and the
  schema is one element's styling surface: splitting it to get under Theme
  Check's count of 40 would split the thing the settings style.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% # theme-check-disable ExcessiveSettingsCount %}
{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:blocks.comparison_column.name",
  "tag": null,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "_comparison-cell"
    }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:blocks.comparison_column.paragraphs.blocks"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "role",
      "label": "t:blocks.comparison_column.settings.role.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "features",
          "label": "t:blocks.comparison_column.settings.role.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "brand",
          "label": "t:blocks.comparison_column.settings.role.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "product",
          "label": "t:blocks.comparison_column.settings.role.options__3.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "product"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "name",
      "label": "t:blocks.comparison_column.settings.name.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.comparison_column.settings.name.info",
      "default": "Alternative"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_head",
      "label": "t:blocks.comparison_column.settings.show_head.label",
      "default": false,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.role == 'features' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "head_source",
      "label": "t:blocks.comparison_column.settings.head_source.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "logo",
          "label": "t:blocks.comparison_column.settings.head_source.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "text",
          "label": "t:blocks.comparison_column.settings.head_source.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "none",
          "label": "t:shared.options.none"
        }
      ],
      "default": "logo",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.role == 'brand' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "logo",
      "label": "t:shared.image.label",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.role == 'brand' and block.settings.head_source == 'logo' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "logo_width",
      "label": "t:shared.layout.width.label",
      "min": 40,
      "max": 200,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 140,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.role == 'brand' and block.settings.head_source == 'logo' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "logo_width_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.layout.width_mobile.label",
      "min": 30,
      "max": 190,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 96,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.role == 'brand' and block.settings.head_source == 'logo' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "chevron_size",
      "label": "t:shared.icon_size.custom.label",
      "min": 8,
      "max": 32,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 16,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.role == 'product' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:blocks.group.headers.layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "cell_alignment",
      "label": "t:shared.alignment.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "start",
          "label": "t:shared.alignment.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "center",
          "label": "t:shared.alignment.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "end",
          "label": "t:shared.alignment.options__3.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "center"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:blocks.comparison_column.headers.divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "divider_style",
      "label": "t:shared.border.style.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "none",
          "label": "t:shared.options.none"
        },
        {
          "value": "solid",
          "label": "t:shared.options.solid"
        },
        {
          "value": "dashed",
          "label": "t:shared.options.dashed"
        }
      ],
      "default": "dashed"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "divider_width",
      "label": "t:shared.border.thickness.label",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 6,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 1,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.divider_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "divider_dash",
      "label": "t:blocks.comparison_column.settings.divider_dash.label",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 20,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 2,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.divider_style == 'dashed' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "divider_gap",
      "label": "t:shared.gap.label",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 20,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 2,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.divider_style == 'dashed' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "divider_opacity",
      "label": "t:shared.border.opacity.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 30,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.divider_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "divider_color",
      "label": "t:shared.border.color.label",
      "info": "t:shared.border.color.info",
      "default": "#0F2E2F",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.divider_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:shared.appearance.header"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_background",
      "id": "background",
      "label": "t:shared.appearance.background_color.label",
      "default": "linear-gradient(rgba(229, 241, 238, 1), rgba(229, 241, 238, 1))"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "border_style",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.border_style.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "none",
          "label": "t:shared.options.none"
        },
        {
          "value": "solid",
          "label": "t:shared.options.solid"
        },
        {
          "value": "dashed",
          "label": "t:shared.options.dashed"
        },
        {
          "value": "dotted",
          "label": "t:shared.options.dotted"
        }
      ],
      "default": "none"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_width",
      "label": "t:shared.border.thickness.label",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 8,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 1,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "border_opacity",
      "label": "t:shared.border.opacity.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "border_color",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.border_color.label",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.border_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:shared.corners.header"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "radius_device",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "desktop",
          "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.options__1.label"
